      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/broccoli/{size}/1861_2.png",
      "created_at": "2012-07-13T20:28:37.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Yeah, it’s also not super-effective vs. an average Chairman turn, because it just changes all of the Operative-&gt;Underboss-&gt;Thug fishing to the start of the turn, and then the thugs deal damage.  However, it is still very effective when you naturally draw an Underboss during the villain turn (as now he/she’ll have to wait to find their appropriate Thug, and it’s super-super awesome when you get a Prison Break (as you’ll resurrect Underbosses, but not their Thugs).</p>\n<p>As arenson9 said, Voss and Dawn are my first thoughts anytime I think of that card.</p>",
